      "reasoning": "My opening hand is:\n\
\n\
- **Swamp**\n\
- **Mountain**\n\
- **Disciple of Perdition** (1B, 1/3 with a powerful death trigger)\n\
- **Dread Rider** (5B, 3/7 with a recursive activated ability)\n\
- **Sling-Gang Lieutenant** (3B, 1/1 that makes Goblins and has a sac outlet)\n\
- **Thermo-Alchemist** (1R, 0/3 Defender with ping and untap synergy)\n\
- **Firebolt** (R, 2 damage, flashback 4R)\n\
\n\
### **Evaluation**\n\
- **Mana Base:** 2 lands (1 Swamp, 1 Mountain) is a bit light, but the hand has playable cards at every turn:\n\
  - **Turn 1:** Swamp + Disciple of Perdition or Mountain + Thermo-Alchemist.\n\
  - **Turn 2:** Play the second land and another play.\n\
  - **Turn 3:** Develop further with Sling-Gang Lieutenant or Firebolt.\n\
- **Power Level:** The hand has strong cards:\n\
  - **Disciple of Perdition** is a great 2-drop with upside.\n\
  - **Thermo-Alchemist** is a solid defensive card that can pressure life totals.\n\
  - **Firebolt** is flexible removal with flashback.\n\
  - **Sling-Gang Lieutenant** can generate value and pressure.\n\
- **Redundancy:** The hand has multiple ways to apply pressure (Disciple, Sling-Gang, Thermo-Alchemist) and removal (Firebolt).\n\
- **Mulligan Risk:** A 7-card hand with 2 lands and playable cards at every turn is **above average**. While the mana is a bit light, the power level of the cards justifies keeping.\n\
\n\
### **Decision**\n\
**Keep the hand.**",
