- **Disciple of Perdition (1B)**\n\
- **Firebolt (R)**\n\
- **Thermo-Alchemist (1R)**\n\
- **Sling-Gang Lieutenant (3B)**\n\
- **Dread Rider (5B)**\n\
- **Thriving Bluff (land)**\n\
\n\
### **Evaluation**\n\
1. **Disciple of Perdition (p10)** is already in play, so I don’t need to cast another one.\n\
2. **Firebolt (p12)** is a flexible removal spell that can deal 2 damage to any target. It’s useful for removing early threats or finishing off a creature.\n\
3. **Thermo-Alchemist (p16)** is a solid defensive creature that can ping the opponent for 1 damage each turn and untaps when I cast instants or sorceries. It’s a great way to apply pressure while defending.\n\
\n\
### **Optimal Play**\n\
- **Cast Thermo-Alchemist (p16)** first. It’s a 1-drop that provides immediate value and can pressure the opponent’s life total.\n\
- **Firebolt (p12)** can be held for later to remove a threat or finish off a creature.\n\
\n\
### **Sequencing**\n\
1. Cast **Thermo-Alchemist (p16)** for **{1}{R}**.\n\
2. Pass the turn to keep **Firebolt** for removal or reach.\n\
\n\
---\n\
