      "reasoning": "I have 8 cards in hand at the end of my turn and must discard down to 7. My hand is:\n\
\n\
- **Disciple of Perdition (p10)**\n\
- **Dread Rider (p11)**\n\
- **Firebolt (p12)**\n\
- **Piranha Marsh (p27, land)**\n\
- **Sling-Gang Lieutenant (p14)**\n\
- **Soulcage Fiend (p31, 1BB 3/2 with a death trigger)**\n\
- **Swamp (p35, land)**\n\
- **Thriving Bluff (p24, land)**\n\
\n\
### **Evaluation**\n\
1. **Lands:** I already have 2 lands in play (Swamp, Mountain) and 3 more in hand (Piranha Marsh, Swamp, Thriving Bluff). I don’t need to keep all of them.\n\
2. **Discard Priorities:**\n\
   - **Piranha Marsh (p27)** is the worst card to keep. It enters tapped, only produces black mana, and its ETB effect (opponent loses 1 life) is minor.\n\
   - **Swamp (p35)** is redundant since I already have a Swamp in play.\n\
   - **Thriving Bluff (p24)** is better than Piranha Marsh because it can produce red mana, but I already have a Mountain in play.\n\
3. **Non-Lands:**\n\
   - **Disciple of Perdition (p10)** is already in play, so I don’t need another copy.\n\
   - **Dread Rider (p11)** is a high-cost creature with a strong activated ability, but it’s not immediately impactful.\n\
   - **Firebolt (p12)** is flexible removal with flashback, so it’s worth keeping.\n\
   - **Sling-Gang Lieutenant (p14)** is a strong 3-drop that generates Goblins and has a sac outlet.\n\
   - **Soulcage Fiend (p31)** is a 3/2 for 1BB with a strong death trigger, making it a great card to keep.\n\
\n\
### **Decision**\n\
Discard **Piranha Marsh (p27)**. It’s the weakest card in hand and doesn’t impact the board as much as the others.\n\
\n\
---\n\
