I already have **Swamp** and **Mountain** in play, so I have access to both black and red mana. I have **1 land drop remaining** this turn.\n\
\n\
### **Evaluation**\n\
1. **Land Drop:**\n\
   - I have 2 untapped lands and 3 playable lands in hand (**Swamp, Thriving Bluff, Thriving Moor**).\n\
   - **Thriving Bluff (p24)** is the best land to play because it enters untapped and can produce red mana, which I need for **Firebolt** and future red spells.\n\
   - **Thriving Moor (p41)** is also fine, but it enters tapped, which delays my ability to cast spells.\n\
   - **Swamp (p35)** is redundant since I already have a Swamp in play.\n\
\n\
2. **Spells:**\n\
   - **Disciple of Perdition (p10)** is already in play, so I don’t need to cast another one.\n\
   - **Firebolt (p12)** is flexible removal, but I don’t have a target right now.\n\
   - **Soulcage Fiend (p31)** is a strong 3/2 for 1BB with a powerful death trigger. It’s a great play if I can afford it.\n\
   - **Sling-Gang Lieutenant (p14)** is a solid 3-drop that generates Goblins and has a sac outlet.\n\
\n\
### **Optimal Play**\n\
1. Play **Thriving Bluff (p24)** for an untapped red source.\n\
2. Cast **Soulcage Fiend (p31)** for **1BB** to pressure the opponent and set up a future death trigger.\n\
\n\
