  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Passed with 2 untapped mana and two castable spells (Disciple of Perdition and Firebolt) in the postcombat main phase while behind on board. MstLg Teach has almost no board presence and is falling behind, wasting an entire turn's worth of mana development.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn with 2 mana unused and no spells cast.",
      "better_line": "Cast Disciple of Perdition ({1}{B}) to develop a 1/3 blocker that can trade with Gravecrawler and provides value on death. Alternatively, Firebolt the Gravecrawler to remove it while the opponent has no Zombies to enable recasting it from graveyard.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 105,
      "player": "MstLg Teach",
      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 10 life vs 20 life, casting Soulcage Fiend is poor because its death trigger (each player loses 3 life) is much worse for MstLg Teach proportionally. The opponent has dominant board presence and can easily kill it. Additionally, casting before playing a land is suboptimal sequencing.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Soulcage Fiend ({1}{B}{B}) without first playing a land",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp first (getting to 4 lands), then cast Sling-Gang Lieutenant ({3}{B}) which provides 3 bodies and a sacrifice outlet with asymmetric life drain (opponent loses 1, you gain 1), much better for stabilizing at low life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 129,
      "player": "MstLg Teach",
      "decision_index": 33,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Thriving Bluff already produces Red natively, so choosing Red as the additional color is redundant - the land effectively only taps for one color. MstLg Teach's hand is heavily Black-dependent (Disciple of Perdition, Dread Rider, Sling-Gang Lieutenant all require Black mana) and they only have 2 Swamps on board. Making this land produce Black in addition to Red would significantly help cast their hand.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Red for Thriving Bluff's color",
      "better_line": "Choose Black to make Thriving Bluff a Red/Black dual land, supporting the many Black cards in hand",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 135,
      "player": "MstLg Teach",
      "decision_index": 35,
    }
  ],
  "blunder_script_version": 32,
}